    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d558">

                <pb facs="0751" n="737" xml:id="pg737"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0019 Control (Korea)/7–3147: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Lieutenant General John R. Hodge to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Seoul</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-07-31">July 31, 1947</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>246. Zurc 978. 49th meeting of Joint Commission held p.m. 31 July for about 3½
                    hours. General Brown chairman. Soviet delegation, when invited to introduce new
                    proposal, reintroduced previous proposals. US delegation restated reasons why
                    these were unacceptable. US delegation then read a letter from certain
                    organizations who are members of Anti-Trusteeship Committees, reaffirming intent
                    to cooperate with the Joint Commission. In modified form, US delegation then
                    renewed its proposal of 47th meeting that Subcommission No. 1 make systematic
                    listing of all applicant organizations showing position of each delegation with
                    respect to each party. Soviet delegation said it would study letter, consider US
                    proposal and reply tomorrow. No change of attitude or progress achieved. Next
                    meeting 1330, August 1.</p>
                <p>Press statement issued by US delegation will be transmitted in clear.<anchor
                        n="47" xml:id="d558-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>[<signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hodge</hi>
                    </signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d558-f1" n="47" xml:id="d558-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram 247, August 1, not printed; for text of statement dated July 31, see
                    Department of State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, August 10, 1947, p.
                    296.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
